Z||000008||rforbes||03-07-2001||01:32 PM||||I'm having a good day as well.  I got my first fiero about 6 weeks ago with a dead engine - a hole in a piston - and spent the last six weeks overhauling the engine.  I also went throught the auto tranny for good measure before I put it all back together.  Saturday I completed the project and fired it up for the first time.  I sounds great!!  It is just the stock 2.5 in an '84 sprot coupe but I plan for my son to learn to drive in this car so I didn't want to go radical..  Anyway,  the car is now at the shop being inspected so I can put it on the road.  I can't wait!!!  About 15 years ago I almost bought a fiero but backed out at the last minute.  Good thing too - it was to be our only car and two weeks later we found out the wife was pregnant.  Now 15 years later my 14 year old son is as excited about this car as I am. :-)<P>Sorry for so much rambling but I am excited!!!<P>Rodney<P>'84 Sport Coupe <BR>Power windows, Sunroof||||reg||7
